 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"SEO Automation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is SEO automation?\", \"a\": \"It is the use of software to perform the repetitive, time-consuming tasks in SEO that someone would otherwise do by hand. Think of the checks your team runs every week: pages that slipped in rankings, internal links that broke, articles that lost clicks. Keep the work that needs judgment, such as choosing what to write next, with your team.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I set up SEO automation?\", \"a\": \"Start with one check your team already runs every week, such as a ranking review, and describe it in Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a>: the data it reads, the limit that triggers it, and who hears about it. Emergent's free tier is enough to build and publish it. Add the next check to the same app with another prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are SEO automation tools used for?\", \"a\": \"They are used to take over the repeated SEO tasks that your team would otherwise do by hand. List your own repeated checks first, then compare each option against that list. With Emergent, the app you build reads rankings straight from the tool that holds them, through its API.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an SEO workflow?\", \"a\": \"An SEO workflow is the order a page moves through, with one owner at each step: research, draft, edit, publish, and a review of how it ranks a month later. Write yours down before automating any of it. Keep SEO and marketing automation apart where the owners differ: when a page exists to bring in leads, the handoff to sales belongs in a sales automation.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which checks should I automate first with SEO automation software?\", \"a\": \"Automate the checks your team repeats most that always end in the same action, such as a page that drops past a set number of places or a title over your length limit. Leave content decisions until later. For local SEO automation, use the same approach per location, with one page list and one owner for each.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best SEO automation tools for an in-house team?\", \"a\": \"The best SEO automation tools for an in-house team read the data you already report on and reach each page's owner directly. Test each option on a month of your own positions and clicks, and count the alerts your team would have acted on. Drop any option whose alerts you would mostly ignore.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need an SEO automation platform or are scripts enough?\", \"a\": \"Scripts are enough while only their author reads the output. Move to an SEO automation platform once more than one person acts on the checks. The rules and their owners then sit where everyone can see them. If the same team schedules posts, build that as its own <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/social-media-automation'>social media automation</a> with its own owners.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is SEO content automation?\", \"a\": \"Here it means automating the checks around your articles, not the writing itself: one check on each draft before it publishes, and one on each published article's clicks afterward. A draft with a title over your limit waits, and an article that loses clicks goes back to a writer. The writing and the judgment about what to fix stay with people.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best SEO automation software for a growing site?\", \"a\": \"The best SEO automation software for a growing site is one whose cost and limits still hold as your page count climbs. Check the price of each run, what the tool does when you reach its cap, and whether you can take the rules with you. Automation on Emergent has no task cap, and paid plans include a full code export to GitHub.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I build SEO automation with Python?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The Search Console API gives programmatic access to the most popular Search Console reports, and its query method exposes the Performance report's data, including clicks and average position. Google's Python quickstart needs Python 3 and a verified site. When drafts start to need an editor's sign-off, give that step its own <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/content-approval-workflow'>content approval workflow</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
